  "description": "MIRSIT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: H3 O1 1+,C130 H114 Gd6 N6 O34 P9 1-,2(C3 H7 N1 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a chain with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.504-4.560 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 136.26-137.19°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [H3O][Gd6(PO4)(AnPO3)8(DMF)6]·2DMF·H2O.",
